diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 96d8ccb..b8005d8 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -78,6 +78,10 @@ Link battles, trades and Max Raids with nearby phones on the same Wi-Fi, or with
 
 Import a mod `.zip` (`romfs/` file replacements, `exefs/*.pchtxt` code patches for 1.3.2) and switch mods on or off in ☰ → Mods. **Order and notes** sets the load order (higher wins), warns when two mods replace the same files, and keeps each mod's readme as its notes. If the game crashes with mods on, they're switched off on the next start. When the mods change, the app translates any new shaders they bring before the game starts (a short wait, once).
 
+### Cheats
+
+Mods → **Cheats** reads Atmosphère cheat files. Import `<first 16 characters of main's build ID>.txt` (Shield 1.3.2: `a16802625e7826bf.txt`), or a zip with the usual `<title ID>/cheats/<build ID>.txt` layout; every `[name]` becomes a switch, with a search box. Cheats that write the game's data (items, money, key-held codes, loops, registers: Atmosphère's code types 0–9, A and C0) work at once and follow the switches while you play; cheats that only patch the game's code are applied when the game starts (marked *Next start*). Unsupported code types (C1–C4, D, FFx) leave their cheat out, logged as `cheats: [name] left out`. Cheats are for single-player: local play is off while any is on, and a crash with cheats on switches them off. Files: `files/cheats/<build ID>.txt` and `files/cheats/toggles.txt` (one `[name]` per cheat that is on). Engine: `dm/host/cheat.c`, `dm/host/cheat_vm.c`.
+
 ## Known gaps
 
 - Nintendo's online services (Surprise Trade, online battles and raids).
